{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790448412,"nonce":"X2TJxR+g8mL2VQ/+vH9HaiMe0dk=","title":"A host that runs ash as a library cannot build a program ahead of time","message":"The one-command build (lower, trampolines, shards, optimise, emit, link) lived in ash_cli's main.rs as emit_aot, so only the ash binary could run it. Caribou runs ash as a library and must build its programs the same way, linking them against its own runtime object instead of ash_runtime.o. Moving emit_aot and AotRequest into ash_core::llvm::aot_build lets both call it. Separately: a crate that depends on ash_std for a wasm target builds ash_std's cdylib too, and that link fails on __wasm_longjmp, which WASI keeps in libsetjmp. Ash's own wasm build never links the cdylib (its script asks for the staticlib alone).","files":null}]}